.TH zclock "" "Command"
.SH NAME
zclock \- GUI clock
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBzclock [\fIoptions\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
zclock -- GUI clock
Usage:	zclock [ options ]
	Settings menu entry (root only) sets the date and time.
.HE
.B zclock
shows an analogue clock face with hour, minute and second hands,
updated every second.
It must be run under the
.B zview
desktop, is resizable, and accepts the standard window
.I options
of GUI applications; see
.BR zview .
.PP
When run by the superuser, the window menu gains a
.B Settings
entry that opens a dialog with two fields,
.B Date:
(as
.IR YYYY\-MM\-DD )
and
.B Time:
(as
.IR HH:MM:SS ),
prefilled with the current local time.
TAB switches between the fields, RETURN is OK and ESC cancels.
OK sets the system clock; if a field does not parse, the dialog
stays up and says why.
The typed time is local time and is converted using the current
timezone.
.PP
There are no other keyboard commands.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR zview ,
.B date
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
On the dialog's message line:
`Use YYYY-MM-DD and HH:MM:SS',
`Year must be 1970-2037',
`No such date',
`No such time',
`Cannot set the clock'.
.SH NOTES
Only the superuser sees the
.B Settings
entry, and only the superuser can set the clock.
The year is limited to 2037 by the 32-bit time counter.
